.TH SVXCONNECT 1 "August 2026" "svxconnect" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
svxconnect \- terminal client for SvxLink reflectors
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B svxconnect
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B svxconnect
connects to a SvxLink reflector over mutual TLS and carries AES\-128\-GCM
encrypted Opus audio over UDP. It monitors several talkgroups at once, shows who
is talking on which, switches between them by priority or by hand, and
transmits.
.PP
It shares one identity with
.BR svxconnect\-qt (1):
the same configuration file, the same client certificate and a shared run lock.
Only one of the two may hold the reflector connection at a time; the other
refuses to start and names the process in the way.
.B \-\-enroll
takes the same lock whenever it logs in to check an existing certificate, and
leaves the check to the connected client when another one holds it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-c \fIfile\fR, \fB\-\-config \fIfile\fR
Use this configuration file instead of the default.
.TP
.B \-\-set \fIkey\fB=\fIvalue\fR
Override one configuration key. Repeatable. With
.BR \-\-init\-config ,
fill that key in the new file instead.
.TP
.B \-\-init\-config
Write a fully commented configuration file, asking for the callsign, email
address and reflector when run from a terminal. It is written to the file given
with
.BR \-c ,
else to
.BR $SVXCONNECT_CONF ,
else to
.IR ~/.config/svxconnect/svxconnect.conf .
An existing file is left alone.
.TP
.B \-\-force
With
.BR \-\-init\-config ,
replace an existing file, keeping the old one as
.IR file .bak.
.TP
.B \-\-enroll
Get the client certificate signed, or check the one you have.
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
With no certificate yet, generate a key and a certificate request, send it to
the reflector and wait for its sysop to sign it. Run this once, before first
use, after
.BR \-\-init\-config .
It retries every 30 seconds and is safe to interrupt.
.IP \(bu 2
With a certificate that is valid here, log in with it and ask the reflector.
If it accepts it, say so. If it refuses it \(em revoked or removed on the
reflector, or the two clocks disagree \(em request a new one with the same key
and wait for it to be signed. If the reflector cannot be reached, say that it
could not be checked.
.IP \(bu 2
With an expired certificate, request a new one with the same key.
.RE
.IP
Exit status: 0 when a certificate is in place (signed, accepted, or valid here
and not checkable), 1 when interrupted before that or when the reflector turned
the login away, 2 on an error.
.TP
.B \-\-headless
Run with no interface, logging events to standard output. This is what the
systemd unit runs.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-tx
Receive only. Useful over SSH, where microphone capture does not work.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-devices
Print the audio devices the backend can see, then exit.
.TP
.B \-\-audio\-test
Loop the microphone back to the speaker with level meters, to prove the device
path works before any reflector is involved.
.TP
.B \-\-dump\-config
Print every configuration key with its resolved value, then exit.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B UP\fR, \fBDOWN
Previous and next talkgroup.
.TP
.B LEFT\fR, \fBRIGHT
Output volume.
.TP
.B SPACE
Transmit. A toggle, not a hold: a terminal delivers characters, not key events,
so there is no key release to detect. Press again, or
.BR ESC ,
to stop.
.TP
.B PageDown
Lock the talkgroup, stopping all automatic switching.
.TP
.B m
Mute or unmute the highlighted talkgroup.
.TP
.B d
Audio device picker.
.TP
.B q
Quit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/svxconnect/svxconnect.conf
Configuration. Create it with
.BR "svxconnect \-\-init\-config" ,
which writes the fully commented example also found at
.IR /usr/share/doc/svxconnect/example.conf.gz .
.TP
.I ~/.config/svxconnect/pki/
Client key and certificate.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/svxconnect/ctl
Control FIFO. Write
.B "ptt on"
or
.B "ptt off"
to it from a script, a foot switch or a compositor key binding.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/svxconnect/svxconnect.lock
The shared run lock.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SVXCONNECT_CONF
Configuration file path, checked before the default locations.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR svxconnect-qt (1)
.PP
Full documentation at
.UR https://svxconnect.app
.UE .
.SH AUTHOR
Written by Joeri Van Dooren, ON6URE.
